{
  "_readme": [
    "Turkish academic term-unity glossary for scripts/tr_style_check.py.",
    "Each entry is ONE concept and the competing spellings a Turkish manuscript",
    "tends to alternate between. The checker never picks a winner for you: it",
    "reports that two variants of one concept coexist, with counts, and leaves",
    "the choice to the author. Term unity is a decision; only the inconsistency",
    "is a defect.",
    "",
    "'en' lists English forms of the same concept. An English form used ONCE is",
    "the standard first-mention parenthetical and is never flagged; used",
    "repeatedly alongside the Turkish term, it is the same inconsistency.",
    "",
    "This file is copied into every project by /new-project. Edit YOUR project's",
    "copy: terminology is domain-specific, and a glossary that fits a machine",
    "learning thesis will misfire on a clinical one. Delete concepts you do not",
    "use rather than living with noise.",
    "",
    "'tr_ambiguous' lists Turkish variants that are ALSO ordinary words. They",
    "are recorded here so the entry stays complete, and they are never counted:",
    "'özellik' means a property of anything long before it means an ML feature,",
    "and a review that writes 'çalışmaların özellikleri' three times has not",
    "drifted in its terminology. Counting them reported term drift in a draft",
    "whose terminology never drifted, and a warning that fires on correct prose",
    "is a warning nobody reads. The cost is real and accepted: a manuscript that",
    "genuinely alternates between 'öznitelik' and 'özellik' is not caught. Move",
    "a word back into 'tr' if your domain uses it unambiguously."
  ],
